## 10. Do not start unrelated features

Do the task that was asked. Do not opportunistically refactor adjacent code,
upgrade dependencies, or "improve" something you noticed on the way. If you
find a real problem outside the scope, finish the task and report it — do not
silently fix it in the same change.

## 11. Stop after the requested scope is complete

When the task is done, stop. State what you changed, what you tested, what you
assumed, and what you did not do.

Before reporting done:

```bash
npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm test && npm run build
```

All four must pass. **Never claim something works because it compiles.** If you
have not run it, say so.

